1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,090
Here's the catch, and it may surprise you.

2
00:00:03,090 --> 00:00:05,760
Rare earths are not actually rare.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:08,455
The rare part is getting them out clean.

4
00:00:08,455 --> 00:00:09,999
There are seventeen of them.

5
00:00:09,999 --> 00:00:12,947
And when you dig them up, you get them mixed together.

6
00:00:12,947 --> 00:00:17,839
Think of them as seventeen brothers and sisters who look almost exactly alike.

7
00:00:17,839 --> 00:00:22,180
Nearly the same size, same habits, almost the same chemistry.

8
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,638
To your eye, and to most chemicals, they look the same.

9
00:00:25,638 --> 00:00:28,547
So how do you pull one of them out of the crowd?

10
00:00:28,547 --> 00:00:30,660
There's no single magic step.

11
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:35,681
You dissolve the mix in acid, and the liquid flows through a long row of tanks.

12
00:00:35,681 --> 00:00:39,162
Each tank pulls them apart... only a tiny bit.

13
00:00:39,162 --> 00:00:40,607
So you repeat it.

14
00:00:40,607 --> 00:00:42,158
Again and again.

15
00:00:42,158 --> 00:00:47,681
A big plant can run hundreds of these tanks in a row, just to get one element clean.

16
00:00:47,681 --> 00:00:49,629
Think of it like climbing stairs.

17
00:00:49,629 --> 00:00:53,497
Each tank is one step... it lifts you only a little.

18
00:00:53,497 --> 00:00:55,917
Want one rare earth, nearly pure?

19
00:00:55,917 --> 00:00:57,995
You climb hundreds of steps.

20
00:00:57,995 --> 00:00:59,850
And that's only the first half.

21
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:01,664
The second half is faster.

22
00:01:01,664 --> 00:01:03,017
Let me run you through it.

23
00:01:03,017 --> 00:01:06,062
Next, the clean rare earth becomes a metal.

24
00:01:06,062 --> 00:01:10,808
You melt it with iron and boron... and that mix is called an alloy.

25
00:01:10,808 --> 00:01:13,409
Then you cool it into thin pieces.

26
00:01:13,409 --> 00:01:18,835
Hydrogen gas cracks those pieces, and you grind them into a powder finer than flour.

27
00:01:18,835 --> 00:01:26,776
You line that powder up inside a strong magnetic field, press it into a block, and bake it at about a thousand degrees Celsius.

28
00:01:26,776 --> 00:01:30,338
Only at the very end do you switch on its magnetism.

29
00:01:30,338 --> 00:01:32,839
That's when you finally have a magnet.

